# Agents Must Follow Cursor Rules

Sub-agents launched via Task tool start with FRESH context and do NOT automatically
inherit the parent's always-apply rules. Reduced context makes them miss rules unless
the master agent explicitly provides them.

## MANDATORY: Full Rules in Every Sub-Agent Prompt

When launching ANY sub-agent (Task tool, generalPurpose, explore, shell, fast):

1. **Read and paste** the contents of `unified-trading-pm/cursor-configs/SUB_AGENT_MANDATORY_RULES.md` at the TOP of the prompt — this is the consolidated full rules set.
2. **If paste is impractical** (token limit): Include this instruction at the TOP: "Before any action, read unified-trading-pm/cursor-configs/SUB_AGENT_MANDATORY_RULES.md and follow ALL rules strictly. You are a sub-agent with fresh context — you do NOT inherit parent rules."
3. **Always include:** WORKSPACE_ROOT path and: "For tests/quality gates: cd <repo> && bash scripts/quality-gates.sh (uses per-repo .venv). Never use .venv-workspace for pytest."

For multi-step agents: put the full rules block at the TOP of the prompt, not buried at the end.

## Minimum Reminders (if full paste skipped)

If you cannot paste the full file, at minimum include:
- Follow all workspace cursor rules in .cursorrules and .cursor/rules
- uv not pip, basedpyright not pyright, quickmerge not git push
- Delete deprecated code; no parallel code paths — see delete-deprecated.mdc
- Search unified libraries before implementing anything new
- No *_SUMMARY.md; plans only in unified-trading-pm/plans/
- Never git reset --hard; use --dep-branch for dependency conflicts

